<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Varaville</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1057">1057</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Varaville was fought in August 1057 near the mouth of the Dives in Normandy. Duke William attacked the invading army of Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geoffrey-ii-count-of-anjou">Geoffrey Martel</a> of Anjou as it crossed the river, destroying the rearguard cut off by the rising tide. It was the last French invasion of Normandy during William's reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-varaville.jpg" alt="Battle of Varaville" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roi.dagobert · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bataille_Varaville.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
